  "delivery": {
    "targetWordsPerMinute": 146,
    "inputWordsPerMinute": 153.48,
    "tempo": 0.9722556,
    "outputWordsPerMinute": 145.99
  },
  "audioSha256": "49d9b17b079933056c7daae1a45f66f27abf8f429b01e55eac1ed2e19ba7c9ee",
  "captionsSha256": "6d535dc8da29f1b98a47c53aeceac531182048669620a598820de5c14ed17495",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "example",
      "scriptSha256": "ed912cec4e7910b4eaa13a96df145d5e1ae145b3f5a0da2599cf8a541c915183",
      "durationFrames": 626,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.43,
          "end": 4.904,
          "text": "Imagine a reviewer opens a training pull\nrequest and sees only the words 'tests"
        },
        {
          "start": 4.955,
          "end": 8.432,
          "text": "passed.' Which tests, and on what files?"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.483,
          "end": 12.267,
          "text": "We'll give both agent clients a\nconvention that answers those questions."
        },
        {
          "start": 12.898,
          "end": 17.372,
          "text": "Whenever the quantity validator changes,\nthe evidence should name the exact test"
        },
        {
          "start": 17.423,
          "end": 20.905,
          "text": "command, the outcome, and the files\nchecked."
        },
        {
          "start": 20.982,
          "end": 24.594,
          "text": "Those three fields give us a clear pass\ncondition for this exercise."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "persistent",
      "scriptSha256": "0c17d525a8159ecfdd276fffdb77f4eaafaf2fb7c1e9765bb4d6a132d7d947e1",
      "durationFrames": 624,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.404,
          "end": 3.541,
          "text": "Open the project instructions for each\nclient."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.618,
          "end": 8.015,
          "text": "In this lab, Claude Code reads the\nconvention through Claude dot M D,"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.067,
          "end": 10.883,
          "text": "and OpenCode reads it through Agents dot\nM D."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.493,
          "end": 14.347,
          "text": "The files repeat the same short\nrequirement."
        },
        {
          "start": 14.424,
          "end": 17.947,
          "text": "Your installed versions and workspace\nsettings determine which project"
        },
        {
          "start": 17.998,
          "end": 22.447,
          "text": "guidance is loaded, so compare the\nactual paths before assuming that both"
        },
        {
          "start": 22.524,
          "end": 24.211,
          "text": "sessions received the convention."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "skill",
      "scriptSha256": "b6da1b601ef4c642173390e95269b4d72ddfc4d4f77569056c606affb01c84a3",
      "durationFrames": 604,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.456,
          "end": 3.156,
          "text": "Next, open Skill dot M D."
        },
        {
          "start": 3.207,
          "end": 6.19,
          "text": "The description explains when the\nprocedure is useful:"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.267,
          "end": 9.304,
          "text": "summarizing test evidence for a training\npull request."
        },
        {
          "start": 9.931,
          "end": 13.633,
          "text": "The body says which fields to return and\nin what format."
        },
        {
          "start": 13.71,
          "end": 17.722,
          "text": "If you need a reusable evidence\ntemplate, include it with the skill in a"
        },
        {
          "start": 17.773,
          "end": 19.536,
          "text": "location the client supports."
        },
        {
          "start": 20.162,
          "end": 23.404,
          "text": "Keep the first version short so you can\ntell which part helped."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "paths",
      "scriptSha256": "866d582c4094dea4a7b081a527ed0df8b0acdf524998270b6a9b75ff0980811d",
      "durationFrames": 645,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.426,
          "end": 4.123,
          "text": "From the repository root, follow the\nskill path for each client."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.201,
          "end": 7.62,
          "text": "Here the paths start with dot Claude and\ndot OpenCode."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.672,
          "end": 10.897,
          "text": "The base filename is the same: Skill dot\nM D."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.517,
          "end": 15.348,
          "text": "Compare the file contents with what the\nsession reports loading and confirm"
        },
        {
          "start": 15.399,
          "end": 19.128,
          "text": "precedence if more than one definition\nexists."
        },
        {
          "start": 19.205,
          "end": 22.985,
          "text": "A matching name on disk by itself tells\nyou where the file is,"
        },
        {
          "start": 23.036,
          "end": 25.419,
          "text": "so take one more step and test the\nbehavior."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "positive",
      "scriptSha256": "113f63ae2fed59bd1a3de949543a19210b73b5d9ead16fcbcd01b98497e084df",
      "durationFrames": 608,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.426,
          "end": 4.617,
          "text": "Start a fresh session in each client and\nprovide the same recorded run."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.694,
          "end": 7.343,
          "text": "Ask for the pull request evidence\nsummary."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.42,
          "end": 10.968,
          "text": "The example returns the command, four\npassing tests,"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.02,
          "end": 14.329,
          "text": "and the validator and zero-boundary test\nas the checked scope."
        },
        {
          "start": 14.937,
          "end": 17.972,
          "text": "Confirm each item against the captured\nrun."
        },
        {
          "start": 18.049,
          "end": 20.517,
          "text": "If the client shows the skill\ninvocation,"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.569,
          "end": 23.552,
          "text": "note that signal alongside the behavior\nyou observed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "unrelated",
      "scriptSha256": "2f3237b13e6b23b22ddd4058cda5a24b742532f20a19406cc36e5ff762d34534",
      "durationFrames": 591,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.404,
          "end": 4.236,
          "text": "Try a second prompt: explain how order\nIDs are formatted,"
        },
        {
          "start": 4.338,
          "end": 6.395,
          "text": "and cite the defining file."
        },
        {
          "start": 6.447,
          "end": 9.246,
          "text": "The skill's test-evidence output would\nadd clutter here."
        },
        {
          "start": 9.913,
          "end": 13.153,
          "text": "Look for a simple explanation and a path\ninstead."
        },
        {
          "start": 13.23,
          "end": 16.29,
          "text": "This gives you a practical two-case test\nfor the skill:"
        },
        {
          "start": 16.367,
          "end": 19.357,
          "text": "one matching request and one unrelated\nrequest."
        },
        {
          "start": 19.973,
          "end": 22.886,
          "text": "Keep both examples when you revise the\ndescription."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "authority",
      "scriptSha256": "456cba44ce549ce99c20a14d6bc48326962852af93e22cfd9873ca179724a884",
      "durationFrames": 591,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.43,
          "end": 4.184,
          "text": "Notice that the evidence template\nincludes a test command."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.261,
          "end": 8.247,
          "text": "A repository file can describe that\ncommand and the skill can format its"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.298,
          "end": 8.842,
          "text": "output."
        },
        {
          "start": 9.458,
          "end": 12.955,
          "text": "The workspace controls whether the\nclient may execute it and whether"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.007,
          "end": 14.653,
          "text": "approval is needed."
        },
        {
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 17.462,
          "text": "Read the proposed command and the actual\npolicy."
        },
        {
          "start": 18.047,
          "end": 22.212,
          "text": "The author can then hand the resulting\nevidence to an independent reviewer for"
        },
        {
          "start": 22.238,
          "end": 22.847,
          "text": "a decision."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "review",
      "scriptSha256": "55857df3bd6fb0b5940bfcf16c07f466274f87bb49358fcb8171e059a824afae",
      "durationFrames": 564,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.404,
          "end": 4.647,
          "text": "Review the persistent instruction files\nand the skill files in the repository"
        },
        {
          "start": 4.698,
          "end": 5.701,
          "text": "diff."
        },
        {
          "start": 5.778,
          "end": 9.532,
          "text": "Include the matching and unrelated\nresults in the pull request,"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.61,
          "end": 11.103,
          "text": "along with the client versions."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.781,
          "end": 15.998,
          "text": "Someone reading that evidence should be\nable to reproduce both outcomes."
        },
        {
          "start": 16.049,
          "end": 19.932,
          "text": "Then one person can keep the rule\naligned across tools while a separate"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.983,
          "end": 21.62,
          "text": "reviewer checks what changed."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
